# Consecrated Sphinx (Bot2's) against Notion Thief (Bot1's): "if each player controls a Consecrated Sphinx, their abilities
# will cause each other to trigger until one player chooses not to draw cards" (its ruling) - and Notion Thief turns Bot2's
# draws into Bot1's. Bot1's turn 3 draw for the turn triggers the Sphinx; Bot2 draws two, each a draw outside its draw step
# that Notion Thief replaces (CR 614.1a), so Bot1 draws both instead. Each of those triggers the Sphinx again, and Bot2
# declines both, which ends it. Bot2's hand is as it was; Bot1 has drawn three cards.

